@spec tv_fx_patch_spec  src=tests/specs/tv_fx_patch_spec.lua  loc=138  cases=10
@exercises dataStore (h.ds), trackerManager (h.tm), configManager (h.cm), trackerView (h.vm)
@surface   ds:assign, tm:rebuild, cm:getAt, vm:saveFxPatch, vm:setFxField, tm:subscribe, vm:loadFxPatch, vm:noteFx
@harness   mk

# Intent
  Pin-tests for the fx patch catalogue: `tv:saveFxPatch` stamps the caret host's
  chain into the project tier of `fxPatches` -- verbatim, by copy, and without
  costing a re-derivation; `tv:loadFxPatch` copies a named chain back out onto a
  host, replacing what it held. see design/note-macros-v2.md § The chain surface

# Helpers
  @fn injectRegion(h, fx)  @ 13-16
  @fn projectPatches(h)  @ 18
  @fn withCatalogue(harness, project, library)  @ 25-30
      -- A region carrying `chain`, with the catalogue's two tiers seeded around it.

# Cases
  @case 'save stamps the host chain into the project tier, verbatim'  [harness]  @ 34-40
  @case 'the catalogue holds a copy, not a live handle on the chain'  [harness]  @ 44-51
  @case 'saving re-realises nothing'  [harness]  @ 55-63
  @case 'a host with no chain saves nothing'  [harness]  @ 67-73
  @case 'the load replaces the host chain rather than appending to it'  [harness]  @ 79-84
  @case 'the host holds a copy, not a live handle on the catalogue'  [harness]  @ 88-94
  @case 'bypass rides the patch onto the host'  [harness]  @ 98-104
  @case 'project resolves over library, and a library-only name still loads'  [harness]  @ 108-115
  @case 'a name in neither tier loads nothing'  [harness]  @ 119-124
  @case 'the whole list lands in one write'  [harness]  @ 128-136

